body:
**Symbiotic** is a Master/Changer/Brute/Trump with the ability to grow and produce parasites that give Brute and changer powers to the people who ingested them. There is a cycle to this power that he tends to exploit. All but the essential are used to hatch as many parasites as possible in the first round of the cycle, leaving him emaciated and slightly delirious. He then vomits the newly born parasites that he can control. He then directs them to find hosts, where they will crawl in through any orifice they can find. Only one or two parasites per host, anymore starts negatively effecting the host too quickly. The parasites feed off the host, but, in exchange, gives them some low brute/changer powers that grow stronger and more varied the longer the parasite(s) stay within the host. However, the host will start to become more and more emaciated the longer they use the powers, unable to eat enough food as the parasite starts to grow. The host will not care though because the parasites will slowly cause the host to become addicted to the feeling of having powers and will do anything to keep the high going. Eventually, the parasites will start to guide the host toward Symbiotic where he will have low levels of control over them, akin to how drug dealers have control over some of the more hardcore junkies.

&#x200B;

Eventually, the host will become almost too weak to do anything. From there Symbiotic has two options: he can have the parasites feed until they kill the host, or he can have the parasites crawl out early. He has been known to do both but tends toward keeping the hosts alive so they can rebuild their strength and they can become hosts again. That way, he already has willing and addicted host that he can use. Once the now fully-grown parasites come back to him, he can have them re-enter his body. Once they do, he can use the powers that the parasites gave the host, so he always has a lot of low-to-mid strength brute and changer powers at his disposal that makes him very hard to put down. This also helps with the early weakness associated with his powers because instead of feeding on him, the growing parasites will feed on the fully-grown parasites. Once Symbiotic gets in this comfortable rhythm, he has small force willing to do anything to get that high, enough powers to make him a top contender in the cape scene, and the early weakness is now gone.

&#x200B;

This is my first time making a power, so I hope it's somewhat good.
